<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fulk Nerra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 970–1040</span> · Also known as Fulk III of Anjou</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fulk Nerra, Fulk III, Count of Anjou from 987 to 1040, was one of the most aggressive princes of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. He built a chain of stone castles, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/langeais">Langeais</a> and Loches, that carried Angevin power into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/touraine">Touraine</a> and against the counts of Blois. Notoriously violent, he also made several pilgrimages to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and founded abbeys.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fulk-nerra.jpg" alt="Fulk Nerra" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges de Manteyer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sceau_de_Foulques_Nerra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
